Keeps public/ present in a fresh clone.

Next.js serves this directory's contents as static assets at the site root,
and the Dockerfile's runtime stage copies it. This project has no static
assets yet (the favicon is a data URI in src/app/layout.tsx), and git does
not track empty directories — so without a file here, a fresh clone has no
public/ at all and the image build fails on that COPY.

Delete this file once real static assets live here.
